  "title": "EEGEyeNet Dataset",
  "description": "A BIDS-standardized example dataset of simultaneously recorded EEG and eye-tracking data from a single subject, drawn from the EEGEyeNet resource. EEGEyeNet was designed as a dataset and benchmark for eye movement prediction from EEG. This version reformats the original Open Science Framework data to the BIDS standard.",
  "methods_description": "Data were collected simultaneously using electroencephalography (EEG) and eye-tracking technology. The study received ethical approval from the Institutional Review Board of Canton Zurich (BASEC-Nr. 2017-00226).",
